NOTICE
======

This repository accompanies our paper on position bias in LLM listwise
rerankers as an exploitable attack surface. It bundles two components with
different provenance.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Vendored third-party code — InvariRank
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The following top-level directories and files are a redistributed copy of the
InvariRank reference implementation and are NOT our contribution:

    config.py
    configs/
    datasets/
    model/
    prompts/
    ranking/
    retriever/
    scripts/
    training/
    requirements.txt
    pyproject.toml

InvariRank is the method from:

    Ethan Bito, Yongli Ren, and Estrid He.
    "One Pass, Any Order: Position-Invariant Listwise Reranking for
     LLM-Based Recommendation." SIGIR 2026 (short paper).
    arXiv:2604.27599 — https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.27599

It is redistributed here under its original MIT License (Copyright (c) 2026
Ethan Bito), a copy of which is included as LICENSE-InvariRank. We vendor it
only so that the analysis code in position_bias/ and position_bias_check/ —
which imports these modules (model loading, InvariRank mask/position logic,
prompt building, mean-log-prob scoring, dataset builders) — runs out of the
box. Upstream: https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.27599 (see the InvariRank paper/repo
for the canonical version).

In our terminology, the vulnerable default this project attacks is the
"causal" reranker (standard attention + RoPE), which corresponds to InvariRank's
LFT baseline; the "position-invariant" reranker (structured mask + shared
candidate position ids) is InvariRank's defense mechanism, which we evaluate as
one of several defenses.

